| `≠` is the exact negation of `=`, and like it is well-defined for any
| two values rather than requiring matching kinds.
let a = 1 ≠ 2
let b = 1 ≠ 1
assert a
assert not b

| Mismatched kinds are unequal, never an error.
assert 1 ≠ "1"
assert null ≠ false
assert 0 ≠ null

| Deep structural inequality, positional for objects.
assert [1, 2] ≠ [1, 3]
assert [1, 2] ≠ [1, 2, 3]
assert { x = 1 } ≠ { x = 2 }
assert { x = 1 } ≠ { y = 1 }
assert not ([1, [2]] ≠ [1, [2]])
